ning  tomorrow  maybe a wee bit of an addiction yeah but  it's a good one  and it's why he's still running despite  a year which could have easily sent  mcgrath back to the bottle one which  included the pandemic and his wife's  lung cancer diagnosis  business was closed my wife's in  hospital diagnosed with cancer  no business no money no nothing coming  in  and  running then  was put in the back burner my hundred  mile run was still in my head  and i couldn't tell anybody just myself  and the man above  i couldn't tell anybody because  you can't go away running and leave your  wife  with cancer to defend for herself  so  it was one hell of a year for not just  me but for the whole world actually for  you though in what you have gone through  will this run do you think feel  sweeter different oh yeah  absolutely yeah this is the run of my  life  it is beautiful here yeah  you told me a few weeks ago that this  was  going to be the run of your life yeah  started and it finished i know god's  good  if he's in charge from here on end  i cannot say enough about this man and  how inspiring his story is i should say  that you can find his documentary on  youtube and itunes right now but man  he's out there running right now i'm  sure he's out there running right now  he's got to get his miles up so tomorrow  he does his 26.2 it's amazing and then  the 26.2 is the last is the last the  last portion of 100 exactly and his wife  is out there and she's his wife is not  there with him his wife is still  battling cancer right now i asked how  she's doing and he said okay sort of a  funny note he said she doesn't quite  know how much he's running right now she  knows he went to do a charity run he  said to me she might find out from  watching your show i don't know but  she'll find out after that i did the  hundred miles rudiment rudemont as we  all are thank you dana well
 

